ALARM(2)                       P32W Unix                        ALARM(2)

NAME
       alarm - schedule an alarm signal

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       unsigned alarm(unsigned secs);

DESCRIPTION
       alarm arranges for SIGALRM to be sent to the calling process
       after secs seconds, replacing any alarm already set. alarm(0)
       cancels the alarm. The alarm is checked at every clock tick
       (1/50 s). SIGALRM kills the process unless it is caught or
       ignored (signal(2)).

       An alarm is kept across exec(2) but not passed to a child by
       fork(2).

RETURN VALUE
       The number of whole seconds that were left on the previous
       alarm (rounded down), or 0 if there was none.

SEE ALSO
       pause(2), signal(2), sleep(1)

BUGS
       An alarm with less than a second left reports 0, the same as
       none. The library's sleep is built on alarm and pause and
       uses up any alarm the caller had set.
